    "evidence_text": "Macroclinium\n\n It contains about 30-40 species native to the tropical Western Hemisphere.\n\nAbronia (plant)\n\n They are closely allied with \"Tripterocalyx\".\n\nUncaria\n\nUncaria is a genus of flowering plants in the family Rubiaceae.\n\n It has about 40 species.\n\n The latter two names are shared with several other plants.\n\n The type species for the genus is \"Uncaria guianensis.\n\nAbronia villosa\n\n It is in the four o'clock plant family (Nyctaginaceae).\n\nOctarrhena is a genus of flowering plants from the orchid family, Orchidaceae.\n\nManglietia\nManglietia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Magnoliaceae.\n There are about 40 species native to Asia.\n\nAbronia maritima\n\nJumellea\n\n In horticulture, it is often abbreviated Jum.\n\nAjuga\n\n They grow to 5\u201350\u00a0cm tall, with opposite leaves.\n\nAbronia turbinata\n\n It is native to eastern California and Oregon and western Nevada, where it grows in desert and plateau scrub.",
